  <item>
    <title>Spartanburg County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/spartanburg-county-sc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-spartanburg-county-sc</guid>
    <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>1-year moratorium (extendable by council vote), no dissent on first reading. Pending ordinance doctrine invoked to halt applications immediately. Exempts previously approved Kohler Plant site project</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>York County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/york-county-sc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-york-county-sc</guid>
    <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>9-month moratorium in unincorporated areas, final reading. Does NOT affect QTS project near Lake Wylie (vested rights). Studies: rate-making, generators, geothermal/heat, noise</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Newberry County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/newberry-county-sc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-newberry-county-sc</guid>
    <pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>12-month moratorium on accepting new data-center permits, confirmed unanimously after the council unanimously denied the &#x27;Project Altair&#x27; land-sale ordinance in June. Staff directed to research appropriate locations for future data-center development.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Colleton County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/colleton-county-sc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-colleton-county-sc</guid>
    <pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>6-month moratorium on special exceptions, conditional-use approvals, and other land-use/development approvals for data centers (Ordinance 26-O-04), adopted unanimously. Planning Commission separately approved a &#x27;digital infrastructure overlay district&#x27; text amendment.</description>
  </item>
